module gunbc.rung_drop.p256_verify_eval_step_count_has_no_in_language_reader

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, Enumerated, DeletedWithoutReplacement }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }

// ============================================================================================
// THE DECLARED RUNG DROP for the falsifiability of an interpreted step-cost claim on the members
// of test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness -- the rung p256-verify-cost-cut fell when its instrument
// was deleted and no in-language reader exists to replace it.
// ============================================================================================
//
// WHY A RUNG DROP AND NOT A ROW NOTE. gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (no silent regression) states that a declared drop
// carries its restoration trigger as one of its five fields, and the trigger is the only thing
// that retires the drop; a roadmap row's note has no such field, so a trigger written into a note
// is prose a later session cannot read as a standing. The precedented shape is a9af6addff179d24207230b0840882c6de05fe4e,
// which typed the stage0-partition gap the same way: the unreachable half became a RungDrop whose
// restoration_trigger names the missing capability, and the roadmap row's note cites the drop
// rather than carrying the trigger. This row is that shape, and the row it belongs to is
// gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority::p256-verify-cost-cut, retired into a dated report row by the
// same change.
//
// WHAT THE READING WAS, AND WHAT WAS LOST WITH IT. One interpreted P-256 verification is priced
// by its eval steps: the named member the_rfc6979_sample_signature_verifies measured 48,296,785
// steps before the std.bignat cut and 23,635,717 after it (gunb-ai/gunbc#16960, head
// 925a59da22445d22671c7d0e74d7eb2e4a2cdaa8). Both figures came from ONE instrument, claim_batch
// run --hermetic over the single member on a heavy slot, whose [witness] line printed
// eval_steps= for that member beside its cpu and wall and whose /usr/bin/time block printed
// VmHWM. A row whose control was a threshold over that line could be REFUSED by executing the
// run: a cut that did not happen produced a different number, so a false claim of a cut did not
// survive an executed control. That is rung 2 (gunbc.guarantee_rung): a check over a quantity a
// run produces, with the invalid state still writable.
//
// THE INSTRUMENT IS GONE FROM MAIN AND NOTHING REPLACED THE READING. ad5c67a316f6
// (gunb-ai/gunbc#16872, the claim entrypoints cutover) deleted src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs
// and moved callers onto gunbc test. The maintained route still runs claims and still prints a
// per-claim cost line (run_claim_measured reports marginal_eval_steps, fill_eval_steps and
// measured_eval_steps beside cpu), so this drop does NOT claim the number vanished from the
// repository -- it claims the two things that make a step figure into a control are missing:
// NOTHING IN THE LANGUAGE READS THE COUNTER, and nothing ADMITS these members on a route that
// judges steps.
//   (1) NO IN-LANGUAGE READER. std.measure carries the quantity (type EvalStepCount, with
//      eval_step_count and eval_step_count_value, and the eval_steps_per_millisecond ratio) and the
//      host realization keeps the counter (v1_interpreter::evaluator_steps, read by
//      cli_run/claim_execution.rs to build the receipt), but no declaration a claim module can call
//      returns a subject's steps. Measured 2026-11-27 in this worktree at origin/main
//      6052ff4a8e4771cff9ac8109bc685f329039411d, three ways: the quantity's two constructors are
//      declared only in dag/std/measure.dag:495, :1518 and :1522; EVERY call site of
//      eval_step_count in dag hands it a number someone wrote -- test.claim.floor_eval_step_budget_witness
//      tier_probe_steps returns the literal 150000, test.claim.floor_cost_distribution_witness
//      builds its rows from 9000, 4000, 900, 4400 and 163840 -- and not one of them reads a run;
//      and over src/v1/stage0/src no host builtin is registered under any name containing cost,
//      measure, steps or profil, so there is no seam a .dag call could reach. So a claim cannot
//      assert its own cost, and a row cannot state a step threshold as something a claim executes.
//   (2) NO ADMITTING ROUTE FOR THESE MEMBERS. The floor's per-claim ceiling is 361,500 eval steps
//      (v2.workflow.required_floor claim_ceiling_eval_step_budget at GrandfatheredTier: the 500 ms
//      of required_floor_claim_work_envelope_ms at the 723 steps/ms pinned in
//      v2.workflow.floor_eval_step_calibration, the NewWitnessTier ceiling being 100 ms of the
//      same rate); the cut member sits at 23,635,717, more than 65 times over it, and the
//      limb-multiply floor of about 1.57M steps is 4.3x over the budget, so no bignat cut brings a
//      verification inside it and the priced members are not enrolled. That leaves the figure as a
//      host-side print a person reads, not a verdict a route renders.
//
// WHAT THE DROP COVERS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It covers the falsifiability of a step figure for the
// twelve members enumerated below, and only that. It does NOT lower any floor ceiling, does NOT
// re-enrol anything, does NOT touch the verdicts (the members still execute and still reach PASS or
// the expected refusal on the maintained route), does NOT cover the per-claim cost line the
// maintained route prints, and does NOT make the recorded figures wrong -- they were executed, from
// one binary, and they are reported verbatim on the row. It also does not cover the CPU or wall
// side of the same claims: that drop is gunbc.rung_drop.floor_cost_cpu_regression_at_constant_eval_steps,
// a different loss on a different quantity.
//
// WHY THE FIGURES ON THE ROW DO NOT CLOSE THIS GAP. #16960's pair is re-runnable only from the
// carried claim_batch built at tree 91d657a62d72 (sha256
// a10ce5fba2d7b87de5d6b65d8c6afa7aa8a4218f966771b3b2efe01d87ac77ff -- a file hash of a binary, not a commit, and it resolves in no git object
// database; it is quoted as the name recorded in gunb-ai/gunbc#16960's prose -- held under
// /home/briansrls/scratch/keen-pike-826 on srv1), whose source is deleted at main and which no
// manifest under the shared names directory names -- the manifest line printed beside run24 names a
// DIFFERENT claim_batch, 9cb21df4c20325fc53ba4187cf4c55bd08037862a45d3900c5cc5519e360a177. Re-running
// it reproduces a historical instrument, not a maintained one; 4142c238239 withdrew the word
// released for exactly such a binary on the same grounds. A control that can only be executed
// against a tree no checkout carries is mitigation, which is rung 1.
data p256_verify_eval_step_count_has_no_in_language_reader: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "p256_verify_eval_step_count_has_no_in_language_reader" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "the falsifiability of an interpreted step-cost claim over the twelve members of test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness: the eval_steps figure a row's control judged came from claim_batch --hermetic, whose source is deleted at main by ad5c67a316f6 (gunb-ai/gunbc#16872), and no declaration in the language returns a subject's step count, so the figures survive as a report and no route re-executes the control. Verdicts, ceilings, the maintained route's own cost line and the recorded values are untouched",

  declared: "2026-11-27",

  standing: Standing { declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement,
    population: Enumerated { members: FreeSemigroup { head: "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness the_rfc6979_sample_signature_verifies (the priced member: 48,296,785 steps before the cut, 23,635,717 after, gunb-ai/gunbc#16960)", tail: ["test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness the_rfc6979_test_signature_verifies", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness wycheproof_1_the_malleable_signature_verifies", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness wycheproof_60_the_shamir_edge_case_verifies", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness a_signature_for_a_different_message_is_false", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness the_wrong_key_is_false", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness a_point_off_the_curve_is_absent", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness wycheproof_4_n_minus_r_is_false", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness wycheproof_11_r_and_s_zero_are_absent", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness wycheproof_26_r_equal_to_n_is_absent", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness wycheproof_2_r_plus_n_is_absent", "test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness the_base_point_is_on_the_curve (the one member the required floor carries; named so this population is not read as floor membership)"] } },
    restoration_trigger: "THE CAPABILITY: an in-language eval_steps reader -- a declaration reachable from a claim module that returns the interpreter's evaluator step count for a named subject, the quantity it returns being std.measure EvalStepCount (eval_step_count and eval_step_count_value already exist; the read does not), realized from the same counter v1_interpreter::evaluator_steps keeps and cli_run/claim_execution.rs already reads for its receipt. SUFFICIENT FOR: one claim on main reads the steps of the named member test.claim.p256_dag_ecdsa_witness the_rfc6979_sample_signature_verifies from inside the claim, a RED refuses a claim whose reading is fabricated or absent, and a before-and-after pair over two trees is then decidable by execution rather than by a host line a reviewer reads -- which is what lets a future step-cost row carry a control again, and what this drop's own retirement is read against. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE IT, each of them a tempting shortcut: re-running the carried claim_batch a10ce5fb..77ff from /home/briansrls/scratch on srv1, whose source is deleted at main so a repeat re-executes a historical instrument and not a maintained one; raising the floor's 361,500-step budget, which is refused on this class already (the limb-multiply floor of about 1.57M steps is 4.3x over it, so no budget short of admitting the current cost reaches it, and the budget is not this drop's subject); the natively emitted verifier of its own, which removes the interpreter steps entirely and so leaves a step meter with nothing to meter; or quoting #16960's figures, which are the report the row carries and establish nothing about a route that does not exist.",
  } }
}
